      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="problem">
          <h2>1. Problem: engine coupling and blind QA in 2D/2.5D action games</h2>
          <p>
            In independent action games, interleaving combat rules, seeded encounter generation, collision geometry, and save-state logic inside engine lifecycle hooks (<code>MonoBehaviour</code> or UI widgets) makes fast deterministic testing impractical and blocks portability across engines. Simultaneously, visual regressions in deformed sprites or generated animation cycles go unnoticed when verification relies exclusively on logic assertions without frame-accurate visual diffs.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Brasas</strong> addresses both constraints by isolating deterministic simulation into an engine-free assembly, validating probabilities across thousands of seeds, and pairing unit/PlayMode tests with automated GPU frame capture and side-by-side 30 fps temporal analysis.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="runtimes">
          <h2>2. Multi-runtime architecture: Flutter Canvas, Unity 6.3 LTS, and Roblox</h2>
          <div class="paper-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="en-p16-runtimes">
            <table class="paper-table">
              <caption id="en-p16-runtimes">Table 1 · Brasas implementations audited in the monorepo</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Runtime / Package</th>
                  <th scope="col">Verified scale</th>
                  <th scope="col">Architecture &amp; role</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>packages/meson_brasas</code> (Flutter/Dart)</th>
                  <td data-label="Scale">96 files · 21,107 LOC · 7 test files</td>
                  <td data-label="Architecture">Procedural 2D Canvas engine with decoupled audio backends (8-voice native mixer with watchdog + Web Audio bindings), embeddable in <code>meson_pause</code> and standalone.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>games/brasas-unity</code> (Unity 6.3 LTS <code>6000.3.12f1</code>)</th>
                  <td data-label="Scale">Engine-free <code>Core/</code> + <code>Runtime/</code> + <code>Editor/</code> + 40 test files</td>
                  <td data-label="Architecture">Open first region (7 connected locations), 6 weapons, 4 enemy archetypes, risk-pact shrines, reactive foliage, and 2D control-rig animation with GPU/MP4 QA.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="row"><code>games/brasas-roblox</code> (Luau / Rojo)</th>
                  <td data-label="Scale">11 files · 2,335 Luau LOC</td>
                  <td data-label="Architecture">Client/server split (<code>Simulation.luau</code>, <code>WorldView.luau</code>, <code>SessionServer.luau</code>, <code>Commerce.luau</code>) maintained as a separate exploratory prototype.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p>
            Inside <code>games/brasas-unity</code>, static pipeline scripts (<code>Tools/prepare_content.ps1</code>, <code>Tools/generate_meta.py</code>, and <code>Tools/verify_sources.py</code>) audit audio manifests, preserve deterministic Unity GUIDs, and verify that <code>Assets/Brasas/Core/</code> carries zero references to <code>UnityEngine</code>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="simulation">
          <h2>3. Pure C# simulation assembly, seeded determinism, and Tilo defense</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Engine-free C# domain assembly (<code>Assets/Brasas/Core/</code>):</strong> houses 27 pure-logic modules (<code>RunSimulation.cs</code>, <code>RegionSimulation.cs</code>, <code>EncounterDirector.cs</code>, <code>SecretPacts.cs</code>, <code>LanternTrial.cs</code>, <code>DashTechniques.cs</code>, <code>TiloActing.cs</code>, <code>Vec2.cs</code>) that execute in milliseconds under EditMode.</li>
            <li><strong>Seeded encounters &amp; anti-save-scum pacts:</strong> seal radii scale across <code>88%–112%</code> with 4 formations and bounded wave composition (3–6 enemies; max 2 ranged, 2 chargers, 1 Captor). Hidden shrines deal 4 non-repeating risk pacts driven by deterministic RNG keyed by <code>(seed, shrine, offer)</code> and persisted into the versioned <code>brasas-unity</code> checkpoint so reloading cannot re-roll outcomes; distribution stability was tested across <strong>10,000 seeds</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Captive-flame defense arena (<code>LanternTrial.cs</code>):</strong> completing the Captor ritual launches a <code>9–11 s</code> defense sequence with <code>3.6 u/s</code> movement, <code>6.8 u/s</code> micro-dash (<code>0.12 s</code>), <code>0.88 u</code> defensive flash (<code>2.4 s</code> cooldown), 5 hazard patterns capped at <code>64</code> active threats, and guaranteed safe corridors.</li>
            <li><strong>Composable dash upgrades without permanent invulnerability (<code>DashTechniques.cs</code>):</strong> combines dual charges (<em>Viento</em>), single-hit-per-enemy ember trail (<em>Brasa</em>), and obstacle-validated threshold teleportation (<em>Paso umbral</em>) respecting water, walls, and combat boundaries.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="rigging">
          <h2>4. Continuous 2D mesh articulation (1,353 vertices) &amp; documented negative result</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Documented negative result (rejected generated sprite cycles):</strong> an experimental pass blending 8 generated idle and 8 generated walk drawings (<code>LiaIdleDrawn-v2</code> / <code>LiaWalkDrawn-v2</code>) was <strong>rejected</strong> after frame-by-frame review exposed double-boot ghosting, cape volume drift, and bag shifting. Candidate assets are kept disconnected as a negative baseline rather than shipped.</li>
            <li><strong>Deployed solution (<code>LiaControlRig</code>):</strong> articulates the approved front artwork (<code>LiaWalkNoEyes.png</code>) through a <code>32 × 40</code> procedural mesh (<strong>1,353 vertices</strong>) driven by <strong>13 weighted controls</strong> (feet, knees, hip, 4 cape hem zones, 3 scarf segments, and satchel) without external Unity 2D Animation packages.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated geometric invariants:</strong> continuous position/velocity transitions between stance and swing phases, breathing compensation on grounded feet, rigid hood preservation, independent animated eyes, vertex-tracked ground shadows, and an automated inverted-triangle detector that caught and resolved a flipped mesh triangle during verification.</li>
            <li><strong>Zero-allocation reactive foliage:</strong> trees, ferns, and flowers deform over root-anchored UV-preserving meshes in response to Lía's contact, Tilo projectiles, and thermal shockwaves with damped elastic recovery and reduced-motion compliance.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

