          <p>
            <strong>Reproducible 30 fps temporal audit (<code>LiaTemporalReview</code> + <code>Tools/analyze_lia_motion.py</code>):</strong> each capture records <code>120</code> idle frames, <code>120</code> walk frames, and <code>150</code> start/stop/turn frames (<strong>390 frames</strong>), encoding side-by-side before/after comparison videos (<code>comparacion-*.mp4</code>) from the exact PNG frames while measuring inter-frame jump metrics to flag motion discontinuities.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="limits">
          <h2>6. Explicit technical limits &amp; pending work</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Directional art coverage:</strong> the 1,353-vertex rig provides smooth front-pose motion but does <em>not</em> synthesize side profiles or back views; horizontal turns still mirror the sprite (with a known sharp lateral flip at frame 99 logged in the temporal review).</li>
            <li><strong>Campaign scope &amp; prototype boss:</strong> only Region 1 (7 locations) is playable; <em>El Custodio</em> currently reuses a scaled <code>EnemyKind.Charger</code> prototype, and 4–5 player co-op remains deferred because the current core assumes a single <code>PlayerState</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Target-device profiling pending:</strong> automated suites and GPU captures ran inside the PC editor; mobile APK/standalone builds, sustained frame-time profiling, thermals, and battery consumption on physical phones remain unmeasured. The <code>games/brasas-roblox</code> prototype remains outside the primary Unity deliverable.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
